IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part7`

-- Tests for wa-interpretation-part7.l4 (ss 48 to 60).  Expected values are written from the text.

§ `Tests -- Part VII`

-- s 48
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised and the duty performed from time to time as occasion requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised and the duty performed from time to time as occasion requires` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 49: the holder, an acting officer or one performing the functions; anyone else is not dealt with.
#ASSERT `the person may exercise the power and must perform the duty of the public office` `the person for the time being lawfully holding the office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the person may exercise the power and must perform the duty of the public office` `a person acting in the office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the person may exercise the power and must perform the duty of the public office` `a person performing the functions of the office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the person may exercise the power and must perform the duty of the public office` `a person who is none of these` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 50(1) and (3): the date gate and the s 3(3) exception.
#ASSERT `the other power is also deemed conferred` TRUE (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the other power is also deemed conferred` FALSE (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the other power is also deemed conferred` TRUE (Date 1 7 1984) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the other power is also deemed conferred` TRUE (Date 30 6 1984) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the other power is also deemed conferred` TRUE (Date 1 1 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 50(2): each included power goes with its own power only (4 by 4).
#ASSERT `the power includes the other power` `a power to provide for, prohibit, control or regulate a matter` `to provide for the matter by licensing, registration or the granting of permits, and to prohibit acts whereby the prohibition, control or regulation might be evaded` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power includes the other power` `a power to provide for, prohibit, control or regulate a matter` `to impose reasonable conditions on the grant` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power includes the other power` `a power to provide for, prohibit, control or regulate a matter` `to withdraw the approval` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power includes the other power` `a power to provide for, prohibit, control or regulate a matter` `to express the directions in the form of prohibitions` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power includes the other power` `a power to grant a licence, registration, lease, right, permit, authority, approval or exemption` `to provide for the matter by licensing, registration or the granting of permits, and to prohibit acts whereby the prohibition, control or regulation might be evaded` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power includes the other power` `a power to grant a licence, registration, lease, right, permit, authority, approval or exemption` `to impose reasonable conditions on the grant` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power includes the other power` `a power to grant a licence, registration, lease, right, permit, authority, approval or exemption` `to withdraw the approval` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power includes the other power` `a power to grant a licence, registration, lease, right, permit, authority, approval or exemption` `to express the directions in the form of prohibitions` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power includes the other power` `a power to approve a person, matter or thing` `to provide for the matter by licensing, registration or the granting of permits, and to prohibit acts whereby the prohibition, control or regulation might be evaded` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power includes the other power` `a power to approve a person, matter or thing` `to impose reasonable conditions on the grant` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power includes the other power` `a power to approve a person, matter or thing` `to withdraw the approval` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power includes the other power` `a power to approve a person, matter or thing` `to express the directions in the form of prohibitions` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power includes the other power` `a power to give directions` `to provide for the matter by licensing, registration or the granting of permits, and to prohibit acts whereby the prohibition, control or regulation might be evaded` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power includes the other power` `a power to give directions` `to impose reasonable conditions on the grant` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power includes the other power` `a power to give directions` `to withdraw the approval` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power includes the other power` `a power to give directions` `to express the directions in the form of prohibitions` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 51(1) and (2)
#ASSERT `the person empowered has a discretion to grant or to refuse` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the person empowered has a discretion to grant or to refuse` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the right to appeal against or seek review of a refusal is left in place` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the right to appeal against or seek review of a refusal is left in place` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 52(1)
#ASSERT `a power to appoint includes the power` `to remove or suspend a person appointed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power to appoint includes the power` `to reappoint or reinstate a person appointed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power to appoint includes the power` `to appoint a person to act temporarily during a suspension or inability` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power to appoint includes the power` `to specify the period for which a person appointed holds the appointment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a power to appoint includes the power` `some other power` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a person may be appointed to act temporarily` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a person may be appointed to act temporarily` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a person may be appointed to act temporarily` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a person may be appointed to act temporarily` FALSE FALSE)
-- s 52(2)
#ASSERT `the cause is included in section 52(1)(b)` `illness` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the cause is included in section 52(1)(b)` `temporary absence from the State` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the cause is included in section 52(1)(b)` `conflict of interest` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the cause is included in section 52(1)(b)` `some other cause` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 52(3)
#ASSERT `the validity of the thing done can be called in question on that ground` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the validity of the thing done can be called in question on that ground` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 52(4)
#ASSERT `the powers in section 52(1)(a) to (c) are exercisable` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the powers in section 52(1)(a) to (c) are exercisable` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the powers in section 52(1)(a) to (c) are exercisable` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `the powers in section 52(1)(a) to (c) are exercisable` FALSE TRUE
-- s 52(5)
#ASSERT NOT (`section 52 affects the tenure` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`section 52 affects the tenure` FALSE)

-- s 53
#ASSERT `the appointment is of the person from time to time holding, acting in, or performing the functions of the office` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the appointment is of the person from time to time holding, acting in, or performing the functions of the office` FALSE)

-- s 54(1): three or more persons, majority of them.
#ASSERT `the function may be performed by those who agree` 3 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-29: was ``the function may be performed by those who agree` 3 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the rule that JUST FALSE needs the text's own words (NOTES, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING") applies, and section 54(1) says the function "may be performed by a majority" and does not close the grant with "only", so the answer is NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the function may be performed by those who agree` 3 1 EQUALS NOTHING
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-29: was ``the function may be performed by those who agree` 4 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the rule that JUST FALSE needs the text's own words (NOTES, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING") applies, and section 54(1) says the function "may be performed by a majority" and does not close the grant with "only", so the answer is NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the function may be performed by those who agree` 4 2 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the function may be performed by those who agree` 4 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the function may be performed by those who agree` 5 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-29: was ``the function may be performed by those who agree` 5 2 EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the rule that JUST FALSE needs the text's own words (NOTES, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING") applies, and section 54(1) says the function "may be performed by a majority" and does not close the grant with "only", so the answer is NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the function may be performed by those who agree` 5 2 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the function may be performed by those who agree` 2 2 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 54(2)(a)(i): at least one half of the number provided for, in whole members (fork F9).
#ASSERT `the least number of members that make a quorum, with a fixed number of members` 3 EQUALS JUST 2
#ASSERT `the least number of members that make a quorum, with a fixed number of members` 4 EQUALS JUST 2
#ASSERT `the least number of members that make a quorum, with a fixed number of members` 5 EQUALS JUST 3
#ASSERT `the least number of members that make a quorum, with a fixed number of members` 6 EQUALS JUST 3
#ASSERT `the least number of members that make a quorum, with a fixed number of members` 2 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 54(2)(a)(ii): one half of the number in office, if that number is within the range.
#ASSERT `the least number of members that make a quorum, with a range of members` 7 TRUE EQUALS JUST 4
#ASSERT `the least number of members that make a quorum, with a range of members` 8 TRUE EQUALS JUST 4
#ASSERT `the least number of members that make a quorum, with a range of members` 7 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 54(2)(b)
#ASSERT `the act is deemed done by the association` 5 3 3
#ASSERT NOT (`the act is deemed done by the association` 5 2 3)
#ASSERT NOT (`the act is deemed done by the association` 2 2 3)
#ASSERT `the act is deemed done by the association` 4 3 3
#ASSERT NOT (`the act is deemed done by the association` 4 2 3)

-- s 55
#ASSERT `the power or duty may be exercised again as often as is necessary to correct an error or omission` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power or duty may be exercised again as often as is necessary to correct an error or omission` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 56
#ASSERT `what the word means` `the word may, in conferring a power` EQUALS `the power may be exercised or not, at discretion`
#ASSERT `what the word means` `the word shall, in conferring a function` EQUALS `the function must be performed`
#ASSERT NOT (`what the word means` `the word shall, in conferring a function` EQUALS `the power may be exercised or not, at discretion`)

-- s 57
#ASSERT `the powers of the body are affected by` `a vacancy in the membership of the body` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the powers of the body are affected by` `a defect afterwards discovered in the appointment or qualification of a person purporting to be a member, deputy or alternate` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the powers of the body are affected by` `a minor irregularity in the convening or conduct of a meeting` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the powers of the body are affected by` `the presence or participation at a meeting of a person not entitled to be present or participate` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the powers of the body are affected by` `a major irregularity in the convening or conduct of a meeting` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 58
#ASSERT `whose opinion, belief or state of mind counts` TRUE EQUALS `the delegate's`
#ASSERT `whose opinion, belief or state of mind counts` FALSE EQUALS `the person's who delegated`

-- s 59
#ASSERT `a delegation has the feature` `the delegator may still exercise or perform the power or duty delegated, at any time` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a delegation has the feature` `it may be made subject to conditions, qualifications, limitations or exceptions the delegator specifies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a delegation has the feature` `where it needs another person's approval, it and any amendment of it may be made subject to the conditions that person specifies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a delegation has the feature` `it may be made to a specified person, to persons of a specified class, or to the holder or holders for the time being of a specified office or class of office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a delegation has the feature` `it may be amended or revoked by instrument in writing signed by the delegator` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a delegation has the feature` `where the power is conferred by reference to an office, it does not cease to have effect only because the person acting in the office changes` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a delegation has the feature` `some other feature` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the other function is deemed delegated too` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the other function is deemed delegated too` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the act is regarded as effectually done` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the act is regarded as effectually done` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the act is regarded as effectually done` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 60
#ASSERT `it is done by the Governor with the advice and consent of the Executive Council` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it is done by the Governor with the advice and consent of the Executive Council` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
